description.p:
EXAMPLE 13: Phenyl 4-acetyl-2-deoxy-3-0-(4-methoxybenzyl)-l-thio- -L-fucopyranoside. 

To a solution of phenyl 2-deoxy-3-0-(4-methoxybenzyl)-l-thio-α-L-fucopyranoside (752 mg, 2.09 mmol) in methylene chloride (10 mL) was added triethylamine (1.2 mL, 8.4 mmol), acetic anhydride (0.40 mL, 4.2 mmol), and dimethylaminopyridine (~5 mg). The reaction was stirred at room temperature for 5 h and then poured into saturated NaHC03 (40 mL) and extracted three times with methylene chloride (3 x 40 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. The crude mixture was purified by silica gel chromatography to afford (16) (700 mg, 83%) as a white solid: 

 0.35 (20% EtOAc/petroleum ether); iH NMR (CDCI3, 270 MHz) δ 7.43 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.27 (m, 5H), 6.88 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, 2H), 5.72 (d, J= 5.6 Hz, IH), 5.37 (d, J= 2.8 Hz, IH), 4.65 (d, J= 10.9 Hz, IH), 4.45 (q, J= 6.6 Hz, IH), 4.38 (d, J= 10.9 Hz, IH), 3.89 (ddd, J= 2.8, 4.6, 12.5 Hz, IH), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.39 (ddd, J= 5.6, 12.5, 12.7 Hz, IH), 2.17 (2, 3H), 2.08 (dd, J= 4.6, 12.7 Hz, IH), 1.17 (d, J= 6.6 Hz, 3H); 1 C NMR (CD3COCD3, 67.5 MHz) δ 171.4, 160.8, 138.8, 132.6, 132.0, 130.8, 130.4, 128.4, 1 15.1, 85.6, 73.1, 70.8, 70.3, 67.4, 56.1, 33.4, 21.4, 17.6;
